1. Introduction

	Unlike web, mobile, or desktop applications, IoT software development demands deep expertise in porting applications tovarious RTOS and hardware platforms. Typically, this process can take anywhere from one to six months. OTAinfo drastically reduces this timeline to just a few hours or days.

With OTAinfo, developers can maintain consistent function calls across different hardware, regardless of the underlyingRTOS. Our solution dynamically provides environment-specific libraries, streamlining the porting process and making IoTsoftware development more efficient and scalable.

2. Features

	Imagine a printf function that remains consistent across any OS. In IoT software development, this concept extends to agreater complexity—not just limited resources, but the variety of chipsets.

What if sensors from different manufacturers could be accessed with the same function call? This would significantly expand functionality across all existing boards, enabling true flexibility and scalability.

The OTAinfo library offers:

	Abstracted Communication Layers – Seamlessly manage different connectivity protocols.
	Abstracted Sensor Layers – Use sensors from different manufacturers with uniform function calls.
	Built-in AI Engine – Enhance device performance with real-time intelligence.
	Integrated Self-Defense – Robust security features to protect against vulnerabilities.
        Detect circular motion or Jumps using in built moderately tuned models (included in this bundle)

With OTAinfo, IoT developers can simplify hardware integration, boost scalability, and unlock the full potential of their devices.


3. Installation
     Pre-requisites:
     	1. Arduino IDE setup for Arduino Nano RP2040 Connect
        2. Arduino Nano RP2040 Connect is able to execute blink example

    Install Libraries
	1. Arduino_LSM6DSOX Library for Arduino
        2. WiFiNINA
    Complete secrets.h with proper wifi values
    Note: The .h files from otainfo_library and secrets.h file may need to be copied in project folder.
    Compile the sample code and deploy it on device. It will automatically start running the functions.
    Using the knowledge from sample code, update the application which needs IoT hardware abstraction. 
    Once done, it can be now ported to OTAinfo listed devices with minor or no change with respective 
    OTAinfo libraries. Yay!!

   

4. Usage
       
    The sample code explains the functionalilty of the library.

